{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 55,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give ear to my prayer, O God;\nAnd hide not thyself from my supplication.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Attend unto me, and answer me:\nI am restless in my complaint, and moan,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because of the voice of the enemy,\nBecause of the oppression of the wicked;\nFor they cast iniquity upon me,\nAnd in anger they persecute me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My heart is sore pained within me:\nAnd the terrors of death are fallen upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me,\nAnd horror hath overwhelmed me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove!\nThen would I fly away, and be at rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, then would I wander far off,\nI would lodge in the wilderness. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would haste me to a shelter\nFrom the stormy wind and tempest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Destroy, O Lord, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " divide their tongue;\nFor I have seen violence and strife in the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof:\nIniquity also and mischief are in the midst of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wickedness is in the midst thereof:Oppression and guile depart not from its streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it was not an enemy that reproached me;\nThen I could have borne it:\nNeither was it he that hated me that did magnify himself against me;\nThen I would have hid myself from him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But it was thou, a man mine equal,\nMy companion, and my familiar friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We took sweet counsel together;\nWe walked in the house of God with the throng.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let death come suddenly upon them,\nLet them go down alive into Sheol;\nFor wickedness is in their dwelling, in the midst of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for me, I will call upon God;\nAnd Jehovah will save me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Evening, and morning, and at noonday, will I complain, and moan;\nAnd he will hear my voice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath redeemed my soul in peace from the battle that was against me;\nFor they were many ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that strove",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God will hear, and answer them,\nEven he that abideth of old, [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "The men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " who have no changes,\nAnd who fear not God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath put forth his hands against such as were at peace with him:\nHe hath profaned his covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His mouth was smooth as butter,\nBut his heart was war:\nHis words were softer than oil,\nYet were they drawn swords.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cast thy burden upon Jehovah, and he will sustain thee:\nHe will never suffer the righteous to be moved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.55.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.55.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou, O God, wilt bring them down into the pit of destruction:\nBloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days;\nBut I will trust in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Prayer for the destruction of the treacherous.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. Maschil of David.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
